      "remediation": {
        "description": "Principal has `iam:PutUserPolicy` — the ability to write arbitrary inline policy documents onto IAM users. No IAM Condition key restricts the content of the inline policy, so any grant of this action allows writing admin-equivalent permissions.",
        "action": "Remove `iam:PutUserPolicy` from the principal. If the principal must manage inline policies for service accounts, scope the Resource field to specific user ARNs that do not include the principal itself. Deny at the organization boundary with an SCP.",
        "example": "{\n  \"identity\": {\n    \"kind\": \"user\",\n    \"escalation\": {\n      \"put_user_policy\": {\n        \"present\": false\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n"
      },
